# Agent tooling and local workflow state
.claude/

# Working notes agents exchange with each other — reviews, findings, hand-offs between
# sessions or between different agents. The directory and its README are tracked so the
# convention survives a clone; everything an agent actually writes stays local. Keeping a
# named home for these stops them landing in the repo root, where `git add -A` sweeps them
# into unrelated commits.
/agent-notes/*
!/agent-notes/README.md

